    show: `Whether anything structural remains where a knot was. Holds kept only by the nervous system (the motor switch,
      perception) would likely leave nothing; a vessel narrowed by long holding, a densified layer, an entrapped nerve
      or changed muscle might remain, and would point to the accounts that expect them.`,
    needs: `an anatomist or pathologist · a body donation programme, or post-mortem tissue · ethics review`,
  },
  {
    stage: 'with-knots-found',
    prong: 'knots',
    title: 'Whether animals have knots',
    design: `Comparative (veterinary): a survey, examination by instrument, and opportunistic necropsy`,
    what: `Veterinarians and animal bodyworkers might be asked whether they find knots in horses, dogs or other animals,
